The web app's content security policy blocks string evaluation. emnapi 2
probes `new Function()` each time it detects a context's features, and the
regex-set, aho-corasick and fuzzy-search WASM packages load it in the browser,
so every page using them reported a violation. Under the policy the probe
already failed, which selects the fallback that names functions with
`Object.defineProperty`; the module now selects it without probing.
Browser regression: apps/web/e2e/specs/content-security-policy-surfaces.spec.ts.

